      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MASTER LOUEY (2) led and fought well when runner-up here last time out, beaten a head. That was his fourth placing from his last five starts so he looks close to a win. Likely to get the favours from this nice draw. Primary contender. EL LAZZAR (7) produced a strong performance at his latest appearance when he scored by 4.3 metres at Melton, his second success from his last three starts. Tactics will be crucial from this wide draw but he is going well. BELLA LOUISE (5) led from a similar barrier to win the last time she raced here and had done well to place from tough barriers in both outings since. BLACK OPAL JACK (10) will be fitter and must be considered after he came from this barrier for third when resuming at Terang.",
